title: Veeam: CDP Jobs
agents: windows
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the state of the Continuous Data Protection (CDP)
 policies of Veeam Backup & Replication and the result of their last finished
 session. If the policy is not disabled, the check also monitors the time
 since the last long-term restore point. For a policy with several replicas,
 the oldest of their latest long-term restore points is used.

 A CDP policy replicates continuously. Veeam closes its session about once a
 day and records in the result of the session, for example, an exceeded RPO,
 failed long-term restore points or a powered-off source VM. The time since
 the last long-term restore point does not reflect the RPO, and it also counts
 long-term restore points that Veeam created incomplete.

 In order to carry out the check, the Veeam agent plugin
 needs to be installed on the backup server. See special instructions in the
 comment section of the two Veeam agent plug-in scripts on how to install
 the scripts.

 - The policy state is {OK} if it is {InitialSync}, {Running} or {Disabled},
   {CRIT} if it is {Failed} or {Stopped} and {UNKNOWN} otherwise.

 - The result of the last finished session is {OK} if it is {Success}, {WARN}
   if it is {Warning}, {CRIT} if it is {Failed} and {UNKNOWN} for any other
   value. For disabled policies, it is only shown in the details and always
   {OK}.

 - The time since the last long-term restore point goes {WARN} if it lies in
   the future.

 You can also configure upper thresholds for the time since the last
 long-term restore point. The defaults are {WARN}: 1 day 6 hours and {CRIT}:
 2 days.

 Older versions of the agent plugin do not send the result of the last
 finished session, and the oldest versions also do not send the time of the
 last long-term restore point. In this case, only the data that is sent is
 shown.

discovery:
 One service is created for each CDP job created by the Veeam tool, including
 disabled ones. To leave out disabled jobs, disable this in the rule "Veeam: CDP
 job discovery".

item:
 The name of the CDP job.
